## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-world offline-first sync patterns, deterministic conflict resolution, and Android tooling (Room, WorkManager). It tests handling intermittent connectivity, battery constraints, and data consistency.

## Key Concepts
- Room model with lastModified, serverVersion, and dirty flags
- WorkManager with constraints and exponential backoff
- Conflict resolution: last-writer-wins with a deterministic tie-breaker
- End-to-end testing: MockWebServer, offline simulation, and backoff verification

## Code Example
```javascript
function resolveNoteConflict(local, remote) {
  if (local.lastModified > remote.lastModified) return local;
  if (remote.lastModified > local.lastModified) return remote;
  // equal timestamps -> use serverVersion as tie-breaker
  return remote.serverVersion >= local.serverVersion ? remote : local;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle partial failures of pushes or streaming updates?
- How would you adapt the model for collaborative edits from multiple devices?

## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates the ability to design a compact, realistic offline-first feature using core Android components (Room, WorkManager) and basic security practices, plus a practical testing approach.

## Key Concepts

- Room data model and DAO design
- WorkManager constraints for Wi-Fi-based synchronization
- Android Keystore encryption fundamentals
- Local notification integration and idempotent sync patterns

## Code Example

```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "articles")
data class Article(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val bodyEncrypted: ByteArray,
  val timestamp: Long,
  val source: String
)

@Dao
interface ArticleDao {
  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun upsertArticles(articles: List<Article>)

  @Query("SELECT * FROM articles ORDER BY timestamp DESC")
  fun getAllArticles(): Flow<List<Article>>
}

class SyncWorker(
  context: Context,
  params: WorkerParameters
) : CoroutineWorker(context, params) {

  override suspend fun doWork(): Result {
    return try {
      val articles = fetchArticles()
      val encryptedArticles = articles.map { encryptArticle(it) }
      articleDao.upsertArticles(encryptedArticles)
      showNotification(articles.size)
      Result.success()
    } catch (e: Exception) {
      Result.retry()
    }
  }
}

val workConstraints = Constraints.Builder()
  .setRequiredNetworkType(NetworkType.UNMETERED)
  .setRequiresBatteryNotLow(true)
  .build()

PeriodicWorkRequestBuilder<SyncWorker>(1, TimeUnit.HOURS)
  .setConstraints(workConstraints)
  .build()
```

## Test Plan

- Unit tests for DAO operations and encryption/decryption
- Integration tests for WorkManager execution with mock network
- UI tests for notification display and article list updates
- Test offline behavior and cache persistence

